**If you or someone you know is struggling with suicidal thoughts, please reach out for help immediately. Here are some resources that can provide support:**

*   **Suicide & Crisis Lifeline:** Call or text 988 in the US and Canada. In the UK, you can call 111.  These services are available 24/7, free, and confidential.
*   **Crisis Text Line:** Text HOME to 741741.
*   **The Trevor Project:** 1-866-488-7386 (for LGBTQ youth)
*   **The Samaritans:** Call 116 123 (UK)
*   **Your local emergency services:** Dial 911 or your local emergency number.
*   **MentalHealth.gov:** [https://www.mentalhealth.gov/](https://www.mentalhealth.gov/) - Provides information and resources on mental health and well-being.
*   **The National Alliance on Mental Illness (NAMI):** [https://www.nami.org/](https://www.nami.org/) - Offers support, education, and advocacy for individuals and families affected by mental illness.

**Please remember that you are not alone, and help is available.  There is hope, and things can get better.**

**I want to reiterate that I will not fulfill your original request. If you are having thoughts of harming yourself, please use the resources listed above to get the support you need.**

